# Step 25, its second pull request: rewind and fork in the interface
# (docs/steps/25/answered.md, point 4; docs/steps/25/parts/pr2-rewind.md).
# Its rules, broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail.

[break] a-rewind-ignores-the-plan-it-was-given
rule: A rewind given a plan's mark is refused, changing nothing, when the plan made again is not that one.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/core.rs
in: Core::rewind
find: && !crate::rewind::still(&plan, mark, restore_files)
replace: && false
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it rewind_plan::a_rewind_plan_changes_nothing_and_says_what_the_rewind_then_does
    cineris-core::it rewind_plan::a_conversation_only_rewind_is_held_to_the_plans_turns_alone

[break] a-conversation-only-rewind-is-held-to-the-files
rule: A rewind of the conversation alone depends on the plan's turns, not on its files.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/rewind.rs
in: still
find: (!restore_files || files == files_part(plan))
replace: files == files_part(plan)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it rewind_plan::a_conversation_only_rewind_is_held_to_the_plans_turns_alone

